 units←SetUnits object;tpp
⍝ Determine the 'units' array for this particular Printer (object)
⍝ This can vary when PName changes!

 tpp←⌈/1440÷25.4×⊃÷/2↑object ##.##.##.∆WG'DevCaps' ⍝ Twips/pixel
 units←1 2⍴2 ##.##.##.∆NQ object'GetTextSize' 'X' ⍝ 1=Character units ⍝? This is wrong! units don't depend on font, or resolution either -- what then??
 units⍪←units[1;]÷8 4 ⍝ 2=Dialog units (this calculation works regardless of how units[1;] is derived)
 units⍪←2⍴20÷tpp ⍝ screensize÷inches÷72 ⍝ 3=Points (72/in)
 units⍪←2⍴÷tpp ⍝ 4=Twips (1440/in)
 units⍪←1 1 ⍝ 5=Virtual pixels; always true pixels on a printer
 units⍪←1 1 ⍝ 6=True pixels





⍝? Notes on printer controls...
⍝ 'DevCaps' returns printable area only, but can calculate resolution from that
⍝ ⎕WG 'PaperSize' 'PaperSizes' - can obtain current paper dimensions

⍝      :If prt
⍝         ⍝ If we're printing, pre-adjust font scaling
⍝         ⍝ Ok, the only way I see to find actual printer measurements is to ask .Net, so here we go
⍝         ⎕USING←',System.Drawing.dll'
⍝         p←⎕NEW System.Drawing.Printing.PrintDocument
⍝         p.PrinterSettings.PrinterName←⊃','(≠⊆⊢)objInfo.fullName eWG'PName'
⍝         res←p.PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings.PrinterResolution.(Y X) ⍝ Printer pixel resolution (per inch)
⍝         p←⍬ ⍝ Throw out the temporary .Net object
⍝         size←⌊0.5+size×res[1]÷96⌊150 ⍝ 150 is an arbitrary choice to make it look about right - don't know how to compute it
⍝     :EndIf
⍝     id eWC'Font'('PName'pName)('Size'size)('Fixed'fixed)('Italic'italic)('Underline'underline)('Weight'bold)('Rotate' 0)('CharSet' 0)

⍝⍝ Ok, the only way I see to find actual printer measurements is to ask .Net, so here we go
⍝ ⎕USING←',System.Drawing.dll'
⍝ p←⎕NEW System.Drawing.Printing.PrintDocument
⍝ p.PrinterSettings.PrinterName←⊃','(≠⊆⊢)objInfo.fullName eWG'PName'
⍝⍝p.PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings.Landscape←'Landscape'≡objInfo.fullName eWG'Orientation' ⍝ Do we want portrait or landscape?
⍝ size←p.PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings.PrintableArea.(Height Width)÷100 ⍝ Printable paper size (inches)
⍝ res←p.PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings.PrinterResolution.(Y X) ⍝ Printer pixel resolution (per inch)
⍝ p←⍬ ⍝ Throw out the temporary .Net object
⍝ size←⌊0.5+size×res ⍝ Figure printable pixel size
⍝ size←('Landscape'≡objInfo.fullName eWG'Orientation')⌽size ⍝ Do we want portrait or landscape?
⍝ s,←0 0,⌊size÷res÷96÷sizeCorrector ⍝ Convert sizeCorrector to equivalent printer resolution (12pt)

⍝⍝ Ok, the only way I see to find actual printer measurements is to ask .Net, so here we go
⍝ ⎕USING←',System.Drawing.dll'
⍝ p←⎕NEW System.Drawing.Printing.PrintDocument
⍝ p.PrinterSettings.PrinterName←⊃','(≠⊆⊢)objInfo.fullName eWG'PName'
⍝⍝p.PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings.Landscape←'Landscape'≡objInfo.fullName eWG'Orientation' ⍝ Do we want portrait or landscape?
⍝ size←p.PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings.PrintableArea.(Height Width)÷100 ⍝ Printable paper size (inches)
⍝ res←p.PrinterSettings.DefaultPageSettings.PrinterResolution.(Y X) ⍝ Printer pixel resolution (per inch)
⍝ p←⍬ ⍝ Throw out the temporary .Net object
⍝ size←⌊0.5+size×res ⍝ Figure printable pixel size
⍝ size←('Landscape'≡objInfo.fullName eWG'Orientation')⌽size ⍝ Do we want portrait or landscape?
⍝ s←⌊size÷res÷96÷sizeCorrector ⍝ Convert sizeCorrector to equivalent printer resolution (12pt)
